    {
     "e": "9️⃣3️⃣4️⃣5️⃣",
     "t": "In 9345, the 9 means 9000, the 3 means 300, the 4 means 40 and the 5 means 5. So 9345 = 9000 + 300 + 40 + 5."
    },
    {
     "e": "✍️",
     "t": "Two thousand, one hundred and sixteen is written 2116. And 1094 is one thousand and ninety-four."
    },
    {
     "e": "🃏🃏🃏",
     "t": "To make the LARGEST number from cards 8, 9 and 7, put the biggest digit first: 987. For the smallest, put the smallest first: 789."
    },
    {
     "e": "📏",
     "t": "To order numbers, compare the number of digits first, then compare from the left. 16, 40, 46, 64, 106 goes from smallest to largest."
    },
    {
     "e": "➕🔁",
     "t": "A sequence follows a rule. 135, 145, 155… adds 10 each time, so the next numbers are 165 and 175."
    }
